The goal of our final project is to learn how to use the images provided by the
AI4Mars data set to generate a design matrix, apply one or more machine learning
method to output labels for new images, and compare our results with other
published results for martian terrain classification \cite{AI4Mars_2022}
\cite{AI4Mars_2025}.


\section*{Literature Review}

Our literature review will entail studying two different sets of articles.
The first are the three articles related to the AI4mars project. The first
is a conference paper from 2021 that explains the labeling procedure and trains
a residual network (ResNet-101) to classify new images\cite{AI4Mars_2021}. The second
is a published article \cite{AI4Mars_2022} that applies multiple ML methods of different
capacity to asses which of them is the best at labeling images, but it also assesses the
efficiency and time to label of each method, important due to the hardware constraints of the
computers on the martian rovers. The last AI4Mars related paper \cite{AI4Mars_2025}
proposes a new ML model specific to the challenges of navigation called FASTNAV,
including quick terrain classification and methods for choosing paths across the classified
terrain.

The other set of papers we will study will be related to other image classification methods unrelated
to the AI4Mars project, with the goal to inform which data processing techniques and methods we
could apply in our final project.
